mon
===

`mon` is a fork of bottom by Clement Tsang.

  Upstream:  https://github.com/ClementTsang/bottom
  License:   MIT, Copyright (c) 2019 Clement Tsang -- see LICENSE

The vast majority of this codebase is upstream's work, unmodified. LICENSE is upstream's
MIT notice and is kept verbatim.

What this fork adds:

- An Apple Silicon power widget, sampled via macmon (https://github.com/vladkens/macmon,
  MIT, Copyright (c) 2024 vladkens). Vendored read-only at `vendor/macmon` as a reference;
  the dependency itself comes from crates.io
- A Claude Code metrics widget, backed by the `claude-metrics` workspace crate
- A configurable graph marker, replacing upstream's hardcoded braille/dot pair. This
  resolves upstream's own TODO in `src/options/args.rs`
- An opt-in pixel rendering path over the Kitty graphics protocol

The binary is named `mon`; the crate is still named `bottom` so rebases onto upstream
stay clean. `git remote get-url upstream` points at the source repository.

Issues with the shared code belong upstream, not here.
